    "e770de2abae5e0cbe2e0": "Based on the image provided, here are the visible ingredients for this pizza, separated into dough and toppings:\n\n**Dough Ingredients (inferred from appearance):**\n- Flour (likely high-gluten or “00” flour for Neapolitan-style crust)\n- Water\n- Yeast (for leavening)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil or sugar (common in traditional recipes, though not visually distinct)\n\nThe crust shows characteristic charred spots (“leopard spotting”), indicating it was baked in a very hot wood-fired oven — typical for authentic Neapolitan pizza.\n\n**Toppings (visible only):**\n- Tomato sauce (likely San Marzano tomatoes, given the red color and texture)\n- Mozzarella cheese (fresh mozzarella di bufala or fior di latte, melted and slightly browned in spots)\n- Fresh basil leaves (whole leaves, added after baking or near the end — classic for Margherita pizza)\n\nThis is clearly a **Pizza Margherita**, one of the most iconic Italian pizzas, named after Queen Margherita of Savoy, who reportedly favored its colors representing the Italian flag: red (tomato), white (mozzarella), and green (basil).\n\nNo other toppings are visible — no herbs beyond basil, no vegetables, meats, or additional cheeses. The simplicity is intentional and traditional.\n\n✅ Final Answer:\n**Dough:** Flour, water, yeast, salt  \n**Toppings:** Tomato sauce, mozzarella cheese, fresh basil leaves",
