    "1448b2100e44c269fee4": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BCE, with various dynasties contributing to its expansion and renovation. The most famous sections were built during the **Ming Dynasty** (1368–1644) to protect the empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups. It served as a military defense system, a border control point, and a trade route (the Silk Road).\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing weapons, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Curtain Walls:** The long, continuous stretches of wall connecting the towers, built following the natural contours of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated stone steps and pathways that allow for the movement of troops and supplies across steep terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of kiln-fired bricks, stone blocks, and rammed earth, often bonded with a sticky rice mortar in Ming-era sections.",
    "d39cdf8ff39a287783d7": {"image": "ChineseWall", "prompt": "Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "1448b2100e44c269fee4"}, "digest": "2a0841efd94395e4e1790db31af09607874d5dfe21b0cd2c20ac2f98c798c0d5", "review": {"correctness": 36, "visual_detail": 26, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "Correctness −4 and visual detail −4: it calls the Silk Road a trade route of the Wall and presents rammed earth/sticky-rice mortar as visible material, though the wall was used to regulate trade and those materials cannot be discerned here. Clarity −3: the expanded historical/material list is not concise.", "answer_sha256": "cb6c9284987cb14599dc9fda0ddf132584aac1b2eaf46bb2af7305cad23fa594", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna", "review_source": "/Users/rshishkin/romancone/amd-ai-ops-evidence-2026-10-25/multiuser-joint-rescore-20261027/combined/reviews-luna.json"}, "finish_reason": "stop"},
