    "61082895d7860e624376": "This image depicts a section of the **Great Wall of China**.\n\n**History:**\nThe Great Wall is not a single continuous structure but a vast system of fortifications built, rebuilt, and maintained by various dynasties over centuries, beginning as early as the 7th century BC. Its primary historical purpose was to protect Chinese states and empires against raids and invasions from nomadic groups of various peoples from the Eurasian Steppe. The most famous and well-preserved sections, like the one shown, date largely from the Ming Dynasty (1368–1644).\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Ramparts/Curtain Walls:** The long, continuous defensive walls constructed of stone and brick.\n*   **Watchtowers/Fortifications:** Prominent, square or rectangular structures built along the wall, used for observation, defense, and housing soldiers.\n*   **Stairways/Access Points:** Steep, stone-built staircases are visible, providing access to the elevated sections of the wall and towers.\n*   **Battlements/Parapets:** The top edges of the wall, designed to provide cover for defenders.\n*   **Material:** The construction primarily utilizes brick and stone masonry.",
