    "ac143cba0e91b828e1c0": {"image": "Titanic", "prompt": "Which movie is this? Explain the visible scene briefly without inventing dialogue.", "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "3b9e3e727d303c93ff2a"}, "digest": "331062e41e275357e5e8073ea40221888c91383633dc9a17fa8b71fa50de47e2", "review": {"correctness": 39, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "Correctness −1: the liberation/romance/tragedy framing is interpretation rather than visible evidence. Clarity −2: the extended emotional narrative exceeds a brief scene description; the movie, pose, bow, and sunset/ocean are accurate.", "answer_sha256": "0224bf6814194487dbaf12b972e741145ef7e9ba980a4fd8ebfc1ee29285632c", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna", "review_source": "/Users/rshishkin/romancone/amd-ai-ops-evidence-2026-10-25/multiuser-joint-rescore-20261027/combined/reviews-luna.json"}, "finish_reason": "stop"},
    "68c9de2d19dec6ead731": "Based on the visible ingredients in the image, here are the components needed to make this pizza:\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (likely high-gluten or “00” flour for Neapolitan-style pizza)\n- Water\n- Yeast (for leavening)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil or sugar (optional, not visible but common)\n\n**Toppings:**\n- San Marzano tomato sauce (or similar high-quality tomato puree)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (likely fior di latte or bufala mozzarella, melted and slightly browned)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking, as they appear bright green and unwilted)\n- Possibly a drizzle of olive oil (not clearly visible, but common in Margherita-style pizzas)\n\nThis appears to be a classic **Pizza Margherita**, named after Queen Margherita of Savoy, who was presented with a pizza topped with tomatoes (red), mozzarella (white), and basil (green) — representing the Italian flag.\n\nNo other toppings are visible, so no additional ingredients should be assumed.",
