    "3636729a92323a8454f1": "This image depicts a section of the **Great Wall of China**.\n\n**History:**\nThe Great Wall is not a single continuous structure but a vast system of fortifications built and rebuilt by various Chinese dynasties over centuries, beginning as early as the 7th century BC. Its primary historical purpose was to protect Chinese states and empires against raids and invasions from nomadic groups of various peoples from the Eurasian Steppe. The most famous and extensive sections visible today were largely constructed during the Ming Dynasty (1368–1644).\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Ramparts/Curtain Walls:** The long, continuous defensive walls built along the ridge.\n*   **Watchtowers/Beacons:** Prominent, fortified structures built at intervals along the wall, used for observation, signaling, and defense.\n*   **Stairways/Ascending Paths:** Steep, constructed staircases are visible, allowing passage up and down the steep terrain of the mountain.\n*   **Stone/Brick Construction:** The primary building material visible is stone and brick, characteristic of later Ming Dynasty construction.",
