    "604a1e49cdae260a8aa1": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the historical northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several dynasties, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most well-preserved sections visible today were primarily built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)** to protect the empire against nomadic invasions from the north. It served as a military defense system, a border control mechanism, and a trade route (the Silk Road).\n\n### Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers and Fortresses:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling.\n*   **Crenellations:** The notched tops of the walls allowed archers to fire while remaining protected.\n*   **Battlements:** The continuous raised wall designed to provide a clear line of sight and defense.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated pathways that allow for the rapid movement of troops and horses across rugged terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of local stone, rammed earth, and kiln-fired bricks, which provided durability against both weather and siege.",
    "a8457d15b89cb29c6e20": {"label": "ChineseWall · 95.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Clarity -5: lengthy answer and extra Silk Road claim exceed the concise request.", "Configurations: gemma12-Q4_0-hip-n2-mtp0-q4_0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "604a1e49cdae260a8aa1"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
