    "d0d2684f354f53b8ef8f": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties (most notably the Ming Dynasty, which built much of the stone and brick structure seen today) expanding and reinforcing it. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese empire from nomadic invasions, control trade along the Silk Road, and regulate immigration and emigration.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing weapons, and signaling.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Steep, integrated stone steps and pathways that allow for the movement of troops and supplies across rugged terrain.\n*   **Crenellations:** The \"teeth-like\" structures on top of the walls used for defense.\n*   **Masonry:** A combination of brick, stone, and rammed earth, often featuring a distinct reddish-brown hue in certain sections.",
    "3eeec5377530c9ccdfa4": {"label": "ChineseWall · 95.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Clarity -5: lengthy feature list and repeated historical purpose exceed the concise request.", "Configurations: gemma12-Q4_0-hip-n4-mtp0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "d0d2684f354f53b8ef8f"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
