    "42e242760a17484a9e39": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties contributing to its expansion and renovation. The most significant portions visible today were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)** to protect the empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups. It served as a military defense system, a border control point, and a trade route (the Silk Road).\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Crenellations:** The notched tops of the walls (merlons and embrasures) allowed soldiers to fire projectiles while remaining protected.\n*   **Battlements:** The continuous defensive wall made of brick and stone, following the natural contours of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Steep stone steps and inclined paths designed to facilitate the movement of troops and horses across rugged terrain.\n*   **Gateways:** Arched openings integrated into the walls to control access to specific sections.",
    "3bc4aacd43629b5b3917": {"label": "ChineseWall · 95.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Clarity -5: lengthy explanation exceeds the concise request.", "Configurations: gemma12-Q4_0-vulkan-n2-mtp0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "42e242760a17484a9e39"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
