    "84d17226b7ec78d4833a": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the historical northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several dynasties, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most well-preserved sections visible today were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)**. It was primarily designed to protect the Chinese empire from nomadic invasions from the north, serve as a border control point, and facilitate trade and communication along the Silk Road.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Crenelated Parapets:** The notched tops of the walls provided cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Battlements:** The protective outer walls that follow the natural contours of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated stone paths designed to allow for the rapid movement of troops and equipment along the steep terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of locally sourced stone, brick, and rammed earth, often held together with a traditional lime mortar.",
