    "750ddf74bf3ec20032dd": "This is the **Great Wall of China**.\n\n**History:**\nConstructed over several centuries (primarily from the 7th century BC to the Ming Dynasty), it was built as a massive fortification system to protect the Chinese empire from northern nomadic invasions. It served as a military defense, a border control point, and a means of regulating trade and migration along the Silk Road.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling.\n*   **Crenellated Walls:** The top of the wall features notched battlements (merlons and embrasures) to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated paths that follow the natural topography of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of rammed earth, stone, and kiln-fired bricks, typical of the Ming Dynasty style.",
