    "7234f0e6dbf800aa846e": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the historical northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several centuries, beginning as early earthworks during the Spring and Autumn period (770–476 BC). The most famous sections were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)**, which utilized brick and stone to create the durable structures seen today. Its primary purposes were to protect against invasions from northern nomadic groups, regulate trade along the Silk Road, and serve as a border control system.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick towers used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Crenellated Parapets:** The notched tops of the walls provided cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Battlements:** The high, thick defensive walls designed to withstand siege engines and projectiles.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated stone steps and pathways that follow the natural topography of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of kiln-fired bricks, stone blocks, and rammed earth, often bonded with a traditional mortar made of lime and sticky rice.",
