    "8369c2ba0ca10167529a": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties (most notably the Ming Dynasty, which built much of the stone and brick structure seen today) expanding and connecting different walls. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese Empire from invasions by nomadic groups from the north, while also serving as a means of border control, trade regulation, and communication.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and spotting approaching enemies.\n*   **Crenellations:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Battlements:** The high, thick defensive walls constructed from stone and brick.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated pathways that follow the natural topography of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Gateways:** Structural openings that allowed for the movement of troops and goods between different sections.",
