    "a3d6f6ac37f6aa09dfa4": "Based on the image, this is a classic **Margherita pizza**, identifiable by its simple toppings: tomato sauce, melted mozzarella cheese, and fresh basil leaves. The crust shows charred spots typical of wood-fired ovens.\n\nHere are the ingredients needed, separated as requested:\n\n---\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (typically “00” flour for authentic Neapolitan-style pizza)\n- Water\n- Yeast (instant or active dry)\n- Salt\n- Optional: a small amount of olive oil or sugar (sometimes used in dough recipes)\n\n*(Note: The dough itself is not visible in the final product — only the baked crust.)*\n\n---\n\n**Toppings (visible on the pizza):**\n- Tomato sauce (likely San Marzano tomatoes, crushed or pureed)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (or low-moisture mozzarella for even melting)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking or just before, as seen here)\n\n---\n\n**Optional but common for Margherita:**\n- A drizzle of extra virgin olive oil (not clearly visible, but often used)\n- Sea salt (sometimes sprinkled on top)\n\n---\n\n✅ No other toppings are visible — no onions, peppers, olives, etc. This is a traditional, minimalist Margherita.\n\nLet me know if you’d like a recipe based on these!",
