    "bdf2056c69fda79d8f13": "This is the Great Wall of China, a series of fortifications built along the northern borders of China to protect against invasions. The wall stretches over 13,000 miles and was constructed over several centuries, with the most famous sections dating from the Ming Dynasty (1368-1644).\n\nVisible architectural features include:\n\n- **Watchtowers**: These are used for observation and defense. They are typically made of brick and have small windows or openings for archers to shoot through.\n- **Battlements**: These are the crenellated parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for defenders while allowing them to shoot arrows or fire weapons.\n- **Staircases**: The wall has steep staircases that allow soldiers and civilians to climb up and down the wall.\n- **Brickwork**: The wall is made of bricks, which were laid in a specific pattern to ensure stability and durability.\n\nThe Great Wall is a symbol of China's rich history and engineering prowess. It was built to protect the Chinese empire from invasions by nomadic tribes from the north. Today, it is a popular tourist destination and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
    "8689cbb7556ad7e67844": {"label": "ChineseWall · 95.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Clarity -5: long answer repeats the defensive purpose and adds general heritage claims.", "Configurations: qwen35-MTP-Q4_K_M-hip-n4-mtp1-q4_0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "bdf2056c69fda79d8f13"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
    "67eb513abd3ab26f612f": "This is **Singapore**, captured at dusk or early evening with its iconic skyline reflected in the water.\n\nHere are the key visible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands (left)**: The distinctive three-tower hotel complex topped with a massive sky park. It’s the most prominent structure on the left side of the image.\n  \n- **ArtScience Museum (center-left)**: The white, lotus-shaped building nestled between Marina Bay Sands and the central business district. Its glowing form stands out against the darker buildings behind it.\n\n- **Singapore Flyer (right)**: The giant observation wheel, one of the world’s largest Ferris wheels. It dominates the right side of the skyline, towering over surrounding buildings.\n\n- **Central Business District skyline (center)**: A cluster of modern skyscrapers, including recognizable towers like the UOB Plaza and OCBC Centre, forming the dense urban core between the left and right landmarks.\n\n- **Waterfront (foreground)**: The calm waters of Marina Bay reflect the city lights and sky, creating a serene foreground that frames the entire scene.\n\nThe soft twilight sky with hues of blue and orange adds to the dramatic beauty of this iconic Singaporean vista.",
    "2323e69c82d2c3a43dda": {"label": "Singapore · 94.00%", "paragraphs": ["Which city is this? Identify the visible landmarks and describe their positions briefly.", "Finish: stop", "Correctness -2: UOB Plaza and OCBC Centre are unsupported specific tower IDs. Clarity -4: lengthy scene embellishment.", "Configurations: qwen35-MTP-Q4_K_M-hip-n4-mtp1-q4_0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "67eb513abd3ab26f612f"}, "image": "Singapore", "src": "../media/qengineering/Singapore.jpg"},
    "086a37b61d9ca2295461": "This scene is from the 1997 film **Titanic**, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) are standing on the bow of the ship as it sails through calm waters at sunset. Jack stands behind Rose, wrapping his arms around her waist, while she extends her arms outward in a gesture of freedom and exhilaration. The warm golden light of the setting sun bathes them in a romantic glow, emphasizing the emotional intimacy and shared joy of the moment. The vast ocean stretches out beneath them, symbolizing both the beauty of their connection and the looming tragedy to come.",
