    "a75cfbae330966583baf": "This is the Great Wall of China, a series of fortifications built across northern China. It was constructed to protect against invasions from the nomadic groups to the north. The wall is made of stone, brick, tamped earth, wood, and other materials, and is over 6,000 miles long.\n\nVisible architectural features include watchtowers, which were used for military observation and communication, and battlements, which provided cover for soldiers. The wall also has a series of gates and passes, which were used to control access to the interior of the country.\n\nThe Great Wall was built in several stages, with the earliest sections dating back to the 7th century BC. The most famous section, the Badaling section, was built during the Ming Dynasty (1368-1644). The wall was completed in the 16th century, and has since been a popular tourist destination.\n\nThe Great Wall is a symbol of Chinese strength and resilience, and is one of the most iconic landmarks in the world. It is also a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and is recognized as one of the Seven Wonders of the Modern World.",
    "0a8c8e6a74c3d3b2a847": {"label": "ChineseWall · 88.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Correctness -4: says the Great Wall was completed in the 16th century, which overstates completion; Badaling is given as a historical example, not as the pictured location. Clarity -7: lengthy and adds unrelated heritage claims.", "Configurations: qwen35-MTP-Q4_K_M-hip-n4-mtp1-q8_0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "a75cfbae330966583baf"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
