    "0f43e5dd50290a43e379": "Based on the visible ingredients in the image, here are the components needed to make this pizza:\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (likely high-gluten or “00” flour for Neapolitan-style pizza)\n- Water\n- Yeast (active dry or instant)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil or sugar (optional, not visible but common)\n\n**Toppings:**\n- San Marzano tomato sauce (or similar high-quality tomato puree)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (likely fior di latte or bufala mozzarella, melted and slightly browned)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking, as they appear bright green and unwilted)\n- Possibly a drizzle of olive oil (not clearly visible, but common in Margherita-style pizzas)\n\nThis appears to be a classic **Pizza Margherita**, named after Queen Margherita of Savoy, who reportedly enjoyed it in Naples in 1889. The red (tomato), white (mozzarella), and green (basil) represent the Italian flag.\n\nNote: No other toppings are visible — no onions, peppers, olives, anchovies, etc. — so none are included.",
