    "bed029e503d6b80d4a46": "This is the Great Wall of China, a series of fortifications built across northern China.\n\n**History:**\nThe Great Wall was constructed over many centuries, starting in the 7th century BC. It was originally built to protect Chinese states and empires from various nomadic groups from the north. The most famous sections were built during the Ming Dynasty (1368-1644) to defend against the Mongols.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Several square towers with tiled roofs are visible along the wall. These served as lookout points and defensive positions.\n*   **Battlements:** The top of the wall features crenellations (merlons and crenels), which provided cover for defenders while allowing them to fire arrows or other projectiles.\n*   **Stone Steps:** Wide stone staircases lead up to the wall and connect different sections.\n*   **Brick and Stone Construction:** The wall is constructed from large blocks of stone and later brick, giving it a sturdy appearance.\n*   **Parapet Walls:** The top of the wall has a low wall or parapet, providing additional protection for those walking along it.\n*   **Gates and Passages:** There are openings in the wall that would have served as gates for controlled passage.",
    "05440e7181ca4ff06ea5": {"label": "ChineseWall · 95.00%", "paragraphs": ["Identify this place and explain its history. Mention visible architectural features. Be concise and do not guess the exact section.", "Finish: stop", "Clarity -5: long answer includes more feature detail than the concise request needs.", "Configurations: qwen35-MTP-Q4_K_M-vulkan-n2-mtp1-q4_0"], "text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "bed029e503d6b80d4a46"}, "image": "ChineseWall", "src": "../media/qengineering/ChineseWall.jpg"},
