    "bd3480e3752caa023de5": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a series of fortifications built across the historical northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several centuries, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most well-preserved sections, like the one pictured, were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)**. It was primarily designed to protect the Chinese empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups and to regulate trade and immigration along the Silk Road.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Crenellations:** The alternating high and low sections of the wall's top edge.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated pathways that allow for the rapid movement of troops and equipment across steep, mountainous terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of kiln-fired bricks, stone blocks, and rammed earth, which were often bonded with a sticky rice mortar.",
    "bbf158f9cfec2920bda3": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "bd3480e3752caa023de5"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: lengthy detail on trade, materials, and construction methods exceeds the concise request. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "f906e94ed11316acfefc0cf4afd4f03239e382346dd14dcfece6aefd48cdbcf0", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "1c6dbdfcf18412c72f63": "This is a skyline of **Singapore**.\n\nThe visible landmarks and their positions are:\n\n*   **Marina Bay Sands:** Located on the far left of the image, it is easily identifiable by its three towers topped with a large, boat-shaped \"SkyPark\" structure.\n*   **Singapore Flyer:** A large observation wheel located on the right side of the image.\n*   **Marina Bay Sands and CBD Skyline:** The cluster of skyscrapers in the center-left represents the Central Business District.\n*   **ArtScience Museum:** A smaller, lotus-shaped building visible near the center, nestled between the skyscrapers and the waterfront.",
    "95c75237c02145537f69": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "1c6dbdfcf18412c72f63"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 10, "note": "Full credit: clearly places Marina Bay Sands, the Flyer, CBD, and lotus-shaped ArtScience Museum.", "answer_sha256": "56ab697d7e3c371550b70b685f64cdfd174c52d4cadb9041cb0453899d543163", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "5883788aa2583dbfb4ba": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "607392a8693745d67e2f"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 10, "note": "Full credit: concise and accurate identification and scene description.", "answer_sha256": "ca33c6bf630122807e7e641ee25a5a17bab7b26d8d5de6be48ba3025707d04e6", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
