    "65f7ed4c9c31da49f5dd": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several centuries, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most well-preserved sections, like the one pictured, were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)**. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese Empire against invasions from nomadic groups to the north, while also serving as a means of border control, trade regulation, and communication.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and providing a vantage point for surveillance.\n*   **Crenellated Parapets:** The notched top edges of the walls allowed soldiers to fire projectiles while remaining protected.\n*   **Battlements:** The walkway along the top of the wall, designed for the rapid movement of troops and equipment.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Steep stone steps and inclined paths that navigate the rugged, mountainous terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of kiln-fired bricks, stone blocks, and rammed earth, which allowed the structure to conform to the natural topography of the hills.",
