    "33d8ca03caebfa185de8": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the historical northern borders of China.\n\n### History\nThe wall was constructed over several centuries, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most well-preserved sections, like the one pictured, were primarily built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)**. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups, while also serving as a means of border control, trade regulation, and communication.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and providing a vantage point for surveillance.\n*   **Crenellations:** The notched tops of the walls, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers while allowing them to fire upon enemies.\n*   **Battlements:** The parapets along the top of the wall that provide a walkway for rapid troop movement.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated stone steps and sloping paths that allow the wall to follow the natural, rugged topography of the mountain ridges.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of kiln-fired bricks, stone blocks, and rammed earth, which were often bonded with a sticky rice mortar during the Ming era.",
    "e6106b5edffab713d0bc": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "33d8ca03caebfa185de8"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: lengthy chronology and construction details exceed the requested concise answer. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "dfd2dd66c5fa655843db96e5a10c8b7cdb799fded369b52882cdca0550305b63", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "b827327e0fe5c5bc3f02": "This is a skyline of **Singapore**.\n\nThe visible landmarks and their positions are as follows:\n\n*   **Marina Bay Sands:** Located on the far left of the image, it is easily identifiable by its three distinct towers topped with a large, boat-shaped \"Sands SkyPark.\"\n*   **Singapore Flyer:** Located on the right side of the image, it is a large observation wheel standing prominently against the skyline.\n*   **Marina Bay Financial Centre / Downtown Core:** A cluster of high-rise skyscrapers is situated in the center of the image, between the Marina Bay Sands and the Singapore Flyer.\n*   **Marina Bay:** The body of water in the foreground reflects the lights of the city buildings and the sunset.",
