    "a850f7b6e8d27a2fb9c6": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a historic fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties contributing to its expansion and renovation. The most famous sections were built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)** to protect the empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups. It served as a military defense system, a trade route, and a means of border control.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for surveillance, housing troops, and storing supplies.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Steep stone steps and sloping paths that allowed for the rapid movement of troops and equipment across rugged terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of stone, brick, and rammed earth, often featuring traditional Chinese roof styles on the towers.",
    "cd6def77f434bbc6d520": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "a850f7b6e8d27a2fb9c6"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: repeats tower, battlement, stair, and material details at length. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "8abeeb4e89dc79f736e3d1c9359edc714edb90d24644d38dd9ea66a2c8685c90", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
