    "537a0e0849bd5c80d621": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a historic fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties contributing to its expansion and renovation. The most famous sections were constructed during the **Ming Dynasty** (1368–1644) to protect the empire against invasions from nomadic groups to the north. It served as a military defense system, a transportation corridor, and a means of border control.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for surveillance, housing troops, and storing supplies.\n*   **Crenellations:** The \"teeth-like\" battlements along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramparts:** Steep stone steps and wide walkways built to navigate the rugged, mountainous terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of stone, brick, and rammed earth, often finished with lime mortar.\n*   **Curved Layout:** The wall follows the natural contours of the ridgelines to maximize defensive positioning.",
    "46923adb80e2d4ed777f": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "537a0e0849bd5c80d621"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "visual detail: presents rammed earth and lime mortar as image-grounded materials, though neither can be established from the visible masonry; clarity: extra material and use details exceed the concise request. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "afcb56e5e57f4e181ddbedc981bd9aa88b2eee4a9f2f1ed271ca43cad451e6c5", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
