    "8269473914896c845988": "This image depicts a section of the **Great Wall of China**.\n\n**History:**\nThe Great Wall is a series of fortifications built across the historical northern borders of ancient Chinese states and Imperial China. Its construction spanned many dynasties, beginning as separate walls built by various states to protect against nomadic incursions from the Eurasian Steppe. The most famous and extensive sections were built and reinforced during the Ming Dynasty (1368–1644). Its primary purpose was military defense, border control, and signaling.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Stone/Brick Walls:** The primary structure is a massive, continuous defensive wall constructed from stone and brick.\n*   **Watchtowers/Fortifications:** Regularly spaced towers are visible along the wall, serving as defensive positions, barracks, and observation points.\n*   **Stairways/Ramps:** Steep, fortified staircases are visible, allowing passage along the wall and up to the towers.\n*   **Battlements/Parapets:** The top of the wall features crenellations (though not perfectly clear, they are characteristic of the structure) for defense.\n*   **Integration with Terrain:** The wall is ingeniously built to follow and conform to the rugged, mountainous landscape.",
    "d792398b4d4f1345b05b": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "8269473914896c845988"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: extensive feature-by-feature and materials detail exceeds the requested concise description.", "answer_sha256": "679b00022d7c16b5354d9c104da4b3e3308967c5bd4b4c774c06148529b2aba3", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
