    "8cbc2db99c6c7d3e15e9": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a historic fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties (most notably the Ming Dynasty, which built much of the stone and brick structure seen today) expanding and connecting different walls. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese Empire from invasions by nomadic groups from the north, while also serving as a means of border control, trade regulation, and communication.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and housing weapons.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Steep stone steps and inclined paths that allow for the movement of troops and horses along the uneven mountainous terrain.\n*   **Curtain Walls:** Long, continuous sections of defensive walls connecting the towers, constructed from local stone and kiln-fired bricks.",
    "68b672a61a6d1d02fe02": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "8cbc2db99c6c7d3e15e9"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: the long feature list repeats battlement/wall details beyond the requested concise account.", "answer_sha256": "3cd620df436d6cf635ffcfe50145e510971519239410f75a0f06d9f640605129", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
