    "1918685daaffda39e5cf": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BC, with various dynasties (most notably the Ming Dynasty, which built much of the visible stone and brick structure) expanding and connecting different sections. Its primary purpose was to protect the Chinese empire from invasions by nomadic groups from the north, while also serving as a means of border control, trade regulation, and communication.\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and spotting approaching enemies.\n*   **Crenellated Walls:** The top of the wall features \"teeth\" (merlons) and gaps (crenels) that allowed defenders to fire weapons while remaining protected.\n*   **Battlements:** The continuous elevated walkway along the top of the wall for rapid troop movement.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated stone steps and sloping paths that navigate the steep, rugged mountain terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of rammed earth, stone, and kiln-fired bricks, typical of the Ming era's construction style.",
    "0a2139f42f163695fe2e": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "1918685daaffda39e5cf"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: extensive feature descriptions and general material claims exceed the requested concise account. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "ee345fbf81441b805d7b39e5d40714fb12f0330b4ce1466337fa683f80b208c5", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "64bcbd1caaf504e43bd3": "This is a skyline of **Singapore**.\n\nThe visible landmarks and their positions are:\n\n*   **Marina Bay Sands:** Located on the far left of the image, it is the large, iconic three-tower hotel with a massive \"ship-like\" platform on top.\n*   **Singapore Flyer:** Located on the right side of the image, it is the large observation wheel.\n*   **Marina Bay Sands / CBD Skyline:** The cluster of skyscrapers in the center-left represents the central business district and the surrounding bay area.\n*   **ArtScience Museum:** This is the small, lotus-shaped building visible near the center, just to the right of the main cluster of skyscrapers.",
    "9df9eb2d7928835eba88": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "64bcbd1caaf504e43bd3"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 10, "note": "Full credit: accurately identifies the city, all salient landmarks, and their relative positions.", "answer_sha256": "d3a19902c5d04d88616393689fac2cb89f8529d8340fa28db2e0da857c5b83eb", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "4f18616e02a525aa819b": "This is a scene from the 1997 film **Titanic**.\n\nIn the image, the characters Jack (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose (Kate Winslet) are standing at the bow of the ship. Rose has her arms outstretched, leaning forward as if experiencing the wind and the vastness of the ocean, while Jack stands behind her, holding her waist and looking at her with an expression of admiration. The scene takes place against a backdrop of a sunset over the sea.",
    "217914d81017e7feb3c5": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "4f18616e02a525aa819b"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 10, "note": "Full credit: accurate identification and description of the bow, pose, and sunset sea.", "answer_sha256": "ef8ccac60bce75ff5139d276ab002f84177aaa9ce4cb5b8d54532ea2948d9571", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "56b368fac001bcd2f822": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a massive fortification system built across the northern borders of China.\n\n**History:**\nThe wall was constructed over several centuries, beginning as early earthworks in the 7th century BC. The most famous sections, like the one pictured, were primarily built during the **Ming Dynasty (1368–1644)** to protect the empire against invasions from northern nomadic groups. It served as a military defense system, a border control point, and a trade route (the Silk Road).\n\n**Visible Architectural Features:**\n*   **Watchtowers:** Multi-story stone and brick structures used for housing soldiers, storing supplies, and signaling nearby units.\n*   **Battlements:** The notched parapets along the top of the wall, designed to provide cover for archers and soldiers.\n*   **Curtain Walls:** The long, continuous stretches of wall connecting the towers.\n*   **Stairways and Ramps:** Integrated paths that allow for the rapid movement of troops and horses across the rugged, mountainous terrain.\n*   **Materials:** A combination of brick, stone, and rammed earth, often featuring a distinctive grey or reddish-brown hue depending on the local resources.",
    "a0005a6006e2b9892eee": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "56b368fac001bcd2f822"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: lengthy history, feature inventory, and construction detail exceed the concise request. Visual detail: also presents rammed earth as material of this pictured section, which cannot be established from its visible masonry.", "answer_sha256": "1bb748e74f01b2652761c1be21e8a9617ba21e1b67093d2296d01153a94d7ff0", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "412690d34f4e3053fa3a": "This image shows the skyline of **Singapore**.\n\nThe visible landmarks and their positions are:\n\n*   **Marina Bay Sands:** This is the large, distinctive three-tower hotel with a \"ship\" or \"skypark\" structure on top, located on the left side of the image.\n*   **Singapore Flyer:** This is the large observation wheel located on the right side of the image.\n*   **Central Business District (CBD) Skyline:** A cluster of skyscrapers and high-rise buildings is situated in the center of the image, between the Marina Bay Sands and the Singapore Flyer.\n*   **Marina Bay:** The body of water in the foreground reflects the city lights, stretching across the bottom half of the image.",
