    "41a69daaa021daf78ff6": "This is Singapore.\n\nVisible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands** – Located on the left side of the image, this iconic hotel features three towers connected by a sky park at the top.\n- **Singapore Flyer** – A large Ferris wheel positioned on the right side of the skyline, standing prominently against the twilight sky.\n- **Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay** – Situated between Marina Bay Sands and the Singapore Flyer, its distinctive “durian” shape glows warmly in the evening light.\n- **City skyline** – Various high-rise buildings and skyscrapers fill the central portion of the image, forming the urban backdrop.\n- **Waterfront** – The calm waters of Marina Bay occupy the foreground, reflecting the city lights and sky.\n\nThe scene captures Singapore’s modern architecture and waterfront beauty during dusk.",
    "7370ebc943112db02b94": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "41a69daaa021daf78ff6"}, "review": {"correctness": 33, "visual_detail": 23, "completeness": 15, "clarity": 9, "note": "correctness: misidentifies the visible lotus-shaped ArtScience Museum as the durian-shaped Esplanade; visual detail: gives an incorrect shape and landmark identity for the central building; completeness: the requested museum landmark is not correctly identified. Clarity: ends with a general dusk/waterfront summary already covered above.", "answer_sha256": "d2987f278d152688abb9a1d7dd91e2cf44b2e0f3e04ce1214e6e9d819bee301b"}},
    "49bd429b41d0e6759a6c": "This scene is from the 1997 film **Titanic**, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the RMS Titanic as it sails into the sunset. With their arms outstretched, they embrace the freedom and romance of the moment — a visual metaphor for their forbidden love and the grandeur of the ocean liner. The golden light of dusk bathes them in warmth, contrasting with the looming tragedy that awaits. This scene captures the peak of their emotional connection before the ship’s fate unfolds.",
