    "8d725aaff96d9dabefff": "This is Singapore.\n\nVisible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands** – On the left side of the image, this iconic hotel features three towers connected by a sky park at the top.\n- **Singapore Flyer** – A large Ferris wheel on the right side of the skyline, standing tall against the twilight sky.\n- **Esplanade – Theatres on the Bay** – Located near the center, between Marina Bay Sands and the Singapore Flyer, its distinctive “durian” shape glows warmly in the evening light.\n- **City skyline** – Numerous high-rise buildings fill the background, including modern skyscrapers and residential towers, stretching across the horizon behind the waterfront.\n\nThe scene is viewed from across Marina Bay, with reflections of the city lights shimmering on the water’s surface.",
    "83298853538d56f2674b": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "8d725aaff96d9dabefff"}, "review": {"correctness": 33, "visual_detail": 23, "completeness": 15, "clarity": 9, "note": "correctness: misidentifies the visible lotus-shaped ArtScience Museum as the durian-shaped Esplanade; visual detail: gives an incorrect shape and landmark identity for the central building; completeness: the requested museum landmark is not correctly identified. Clarity: ends with a general dusk/waterfront summary already covered above.", "answer_sha256": "4fb1d628068238784460bf8cbeec66ad6c8f47c57d9a52041e634e3b2a9f700d"}},
    "de2e72b289c89a198726": "This scene is from the 1997 film **Titanic**, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the Titanic as it sails into a sunset. Jack wraps his arms around Rose from behind, and she stretches her arms out wide, embracing the moment with joy and freedom. The golden light of the setting sun bathes them in warmth, symbolizing hope, romance, and liberation — especially poignant given Rose’s escape from her oppressive life aboard the ship. The vast ocean and sky behind them emphasize the scale of their emotional journey and the beauty of their connection.",
    "b461a6ce6ef1ca3c5e0b": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "de2e72b289c89a198726"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: the extended symbolism and Rose’s backstory go beyond the requested brief description of the visible scene.", "answer_sha256": "8763771e7b0c24b10a1b209374973f0b427bd75515a41ec3dea645c4be7d8f16"}},
    "054a05d600e4dd25efde": "Based on the visible ingredients in the image, here are the components needed to make this pizza:\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (likely high-gluten or “00” flour for Neapolitan-style pizza)\n- Water\n- Yeast (instant or active dry)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil or sugar (optional, not visible but common)\n\n**Toppings:**\n- San Marzano tomato sauce (or similar high-quality tomato puree)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (likely fior di latte or bufala mozzarella, torn into pieces)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking)\n- Possibly a drizzle of olive oil (not clearly visible, but common in Margherita-style pizzas)\n\nThis appears to be a classic Margherita pizza, named after Queen Margherita of Italy, who reportedly enjoyed it in 1889. The simplicity of the toppings — tomato, mozzarella, and basil — reflects its traditional Neapolitan roots.\n\nNote: No other toppings (like onions, peppers, olives, etc.) are visible, so none are included.",
    "213d2f0ee02c8b63f342": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "054a05d600e4dd25efde"}, "review": {"correctness": 39, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "correctness: includes a possible olive-oil topping despite acknowledging it is not visible; clarity: adds flour and cheese variants, pizza history, and repeated topping commentary beyond the requested list.", "answer_sha256": "7b6c1d40b42346ad12bf7edf38cbe824ff6cb6650c950446f8e37b1ed49e86bc"}},
    "b13e8dbb41efd3a73430": "This is the Great Wall of China, a series of fortifications built across northern China to protect against invasions. Visible features include watchtowers, crenellated walls, and staircases winding along mountain ridges. The wall's construction spans centuries, with sections built by various dynasties, notably the Ming Dynasty. It symbolizes China's historical defense strategies and engineering prowess.",
    "4a5219aff84223ca4a8d": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "b13e8dbb41efd3a73430"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 9, "note": "clarity: the closing symbolism and engineering-praise sentence adds context beyond the concise history and image description.", "answer_sha256": "8c8dd260cabc26a7137e24dbf724340cb01c132c85df2cf4bb470b50d215aecf"}},
    "15294dd9234c2459959d": "This is **Singapore**, a city-state in Southeast Asia.\n\nVisible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands** – On the left side of the image, this iconic hotel and resort features three towers connected by a sky park at the top. It’s one of Singapore’s most recognizable structures.\n  \n- **Singapore Flyer** – On the right side, this giant observation wheel stands tall against the twilight sky. It’s one of the largest Ferris wheels in the world and offers panoramic views of the city.\n\n- **ArtScience Museum** – Located between Marina Bay Sands and the Singapore Flyer, its lotus-shaped design glows warmly at dusk.\n\n- **City skyline** – Behind these landmarks, a cluster of modern skyscrapers forms the urban backdrop, illuminated as evening falls.\n\nThe scene is viewed from across **Marina Bay**, with the water reflecting the city lights and sunset hues. The overall composition captures Singapore’s blend of futuristic architecture and vibrant urban life.",
    "ec1fc2b9b20396564903": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "15294dd9234c2459959d"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: adds facts about the Flyer’s size and use, plus a repeated summary of the skyline and waterfront.", "answer_sha256": "a4549fe6a2e869c4f4d4549f52a8aee5213ac96f245f11fa6d66bd34f568177e"}},
    "4ece9fe8369859c7627f": "This scene is from the 1997 film *Titanic*, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the Titanic as it sails into a sunset. Jack wraps his arms around Rose from behind, holding her close as she spreads her arms wide, embracing the moment with joy and freedom. The golden light of the setting sun bathes them in warmth, contrasting with the vast, dark ocean below — symbolizing both the beauty of their connection and the looming tragedy ahead.",
    "85e015feb69c58e1a4bd": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "4ece9fe8369859c7627f"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: adds symbolic interpretation of the sunset and looming tragedy beyond the requested brief scene description.", "answer_sha256": "0f828f595937c3512932bb881932825c17b81359a1fe7c03945aabd4726e62c3"}},
    "c5f6c9b2f2b169955cbe": "Based on the visible ingredients in the image, here are the components needed to make this pizza:\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (likely “00” flour for traditional Neapolitan-style dough)\n- Water\n- Yeast (for leavening)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil or sugar (optional, but common in traditional recipes)\n\n**Toppings:**\n- San Marzano tomato sauce (or similar high-quality tomato puree)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (likely fior di latte or bufala mozzarella, torn into pieces)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking)\n- Possibly a drizzle of olive oil (not clearly visible, but often used)\n\nNote: The charred spots on the crust and the puffy, airy edges suggest it was baked in a very hot wood-fired oven — typical for authentic Neapolitan pizza (Pizza Margherita). No other toppings are visibly present.",
