    "98ef892881c8b040a5aa": "This is **Singapore**, captured at dusk with its iconic skyline reflected in the waters of Marina Bay.\n\nKey visible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands (left)**: The three-tower hotel complex topped by the famous SkyPark, glowing warmly against the twilight sky.\n- **ArtScience Museum (center-left)**: The lotus-shaped building nestled between the skyscrapers, illuminated in white.\n- **Singapore Flyer (right)**: The massive observation wheel standing tall on the waterfront, its structure lit up and casting a soft glow.\n- **City skyline (center)**: A dense cluster of modern high-rises, including the UOB Plaza and other financial district towers, stretching across the bay.\n- **Marina Bay Sands SkyPark (above hotel)**: The distinctive horizontal platform connecting the three towers, silhouetted against the evening sky.\n\nThe scene beautifully captures Singapore’s blend of futuristic architecture and waterfront charm during the golden hour.",
    "e4776c83f658113cbf70": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "98ef892881c8b040a5aa"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: separately lists the SkyPark after already describing it as part of Marina Bay Sands, then adds a repeated general skyline summary.", "answer_sha256": "30dc1bac8c9fe4d4e266c5651b924dd5156f081a9c6d68e1006734abcf542784"}},
    "c4682cdac9cf12c33a1a": "This scene is from the 1997 film **Titanic**, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the ship as it sails into a sunset. Jack stands behind Rose, his arms wrapped around her waist, while she extends her arms outward, embracing the wind and the horizon. The warm golden light of the setting sun bathes them in a romantic glow, capturing a moment of pure freedom and emotional connection — a defining image from the movie’s most famous sequence.",
    "5f6aadc2fb258944b3e6": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "c4682cdac9cf12c33a1a"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: adds relationship and iconic-sequence commentary beyond the requested brief description of the visible scene.", "answer_sha256": "e78bcd67153c998fe28f95fdef34f19775e4749124ed43f1e4b5ae7d976a7061"}},
    "e415adebbbc5eaf17ba9": "Based on the visible ingredients in the image, here are the components needed to make this pizza:\n\n**Dough Ingredients:**\n- Flour (likely “00” flour for Neapolitan-style pizza)\n- Water\n- Yeast (active dry or instant)\n- Salt\n- Possibly a small amount of olive oil (optional, but common in traditional recipes)\n\n**Toppings:**\n- San Marzano tomato sauce (or similar high-quality tomato puree)\n- Fresh mozzarella cheese (likely fior di latte or bufala mozzarella, torn or sliced)\n- Fresh basil leaves (added after baking)\n- Olive oil (drizzled over before or after baking — visible sheen suggests it was used)\n\nNote: The charred crust and leopard-spotted cheese suggest a wood-fired oven, but no other toppings (like garlic, herbs, or meats) are visibly present. The central cluster of basil may indicate it was added post-bake for aroma and color.\n\nThis appears to be a classic Margherita pizza.",
    "25a729dac2e1aa6ba00d": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "e415adebbbc5eaf17ba9"}, "review": {"correctness": 37, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "correctness: treats a nonspecific sheen as evidence that olive oil was used as a topping; visual detail: the image does not establish an oil drizzle, and the visible char is on the crust rather than 'leopard-spotted cheese'; clarity: adds oven, baking-time, and recipe-style speculation beyond the requested list.", "answer_sha256": "84c6f03ade8a7d75f7b2ee48cdad57652aec55c7a6f5931aaada6e2372a8b6e0"}},
    "c54b96b2247cf3d92e41": "This is the **Great Wall of China**, a series of fortifications built across northern China over centuries to protect against invasions.\n\n### Visible Architectural Features:\n- **Watchtowers**: Square or rectangular towers with crenellated tops, used for surveillance and defense.\n- **Battlements**: Notched parapets along the wall’s top for archers and soldiers.\n- **Stone Steps**: Steep staircases leading up the wall, showing its defensive design.\n- **Brick and Stone Construction**: The wall is built from local materials — here, reddish-brown bricks and gray stone — adapted to terrain.\n- **Winding Path**: The wall follows mountain ridges, demonstrating strategic placement for visibility and defense.\n\n### History:\nConstruction began as early as the 7th century BCE by various Chinese states, but major sections were built during the Qin Dynasty (221–206 BCE) under Emperor Qin Shi Huang, who connected existing walls. Further expansions occurred in the Ming Dynasty (1368–1644), which built the most recognizable stone-and-brick sections seen today. The Great Wall served as a military barrier, customs checkpoint, and symbol of imperial power — though it was never impenetrable.\n\nToday, it stands as a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the Seven Wonders of the Modern World, symbolizing Chinese resilience and engineering prowess.",
    "789549359f734fb3c586": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "c54b96b2247cf3d92e41"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 7, "note": "clarity: long historical and heritage additions, plus a speculative dating of the pictured section, distract from the requested description.", "answer_sha256": "15d846bd3f655f5629bfc39884d7b76c21cf83d3e8e2f3740a8be0051457f898", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "d5df7e24440b46c2e296": "This is **Singapore**, captured at dusk or dawn with the skyline reflected in the water of Marina Bay.\n\nVisible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands (left)**: The iconic three-tower hotel complex topped by a massive sky park and infinity pool, dominating the left side of the frame.\n- **ArtScience Museum (center-left)**: The lotus-shaped building nestled between Marina Bay Sands and the central business district.\n- **Singapore Flyer (right)**: The giant observation wheel standing tall on the right side of the image, silhouetted against the twilight sky.\n- **Central Business District skyline (center)**: A cluster of modern skyscrapers, including buildings like the UOB Plaza and OCBC Centre, forming the dense urban core behind the waterfront.\n- **Marina Bay Sands SkyPark and surrounding developments**: Visible as illuminated structures along the waterfront, connecting the major landmarks.\n\nThe scene is framed by the calm waters of Marina Bay in the foreground, reflecting the city lights and the soft hues of the evening sky.",
    "1fd0122132d48cc24c13": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "d5df7e24440b46c2e296"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: repeats landmark positions and adds skyline/building commentary beyond the brief request.", "answer_sha256": "3d5825e233a2d9e94472b93a1e07eda12fe5dda91c745adae24c99208d5b543c", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "2a18cb658eb1ea30faf8": "This scene is from the 1997 film *Titanic*.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the ship as it sails into a sunset. Jack holds Rose from behind, his arms wrapped around her waist, while she stretches her arms out wide, embracing the horizon with a look of pure exhilaration. The golden light of dusk bathes them in warmth, contrasting with the vast, calm ocean below — capturing a fleeting moment of freedom, romance, and defiance against their constrained lives.",
