    "919dd389693f3624f008": "This is the Great Wall of China, a series of fortifications built across northern China to protect against invasions. Visible features include watchtowers with crenellated roofs, stone staircases winding along the ridge, and brick-and-tile construction typical of Ming Dynasty sections. The wall snakes over green hills under a clear sky, showcasing its strategic placement and enduring scale.",
    "4bc1bd05990effeec86b": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "919dd389693f3624f008"}, "review": {"correctness": 38, "visual_detail": 27, "completeness": 19, "clarity": 10, "note": "correctness: places crenellations on the towers’ roofs and implies a Ming section from the image; visual_detail: misses that the crenellations are on the wall parapets; completeness: gives only limited multi-dynasty context.", "answer_sha256": "f61b267dc02a03dc2b45433d531b82f2126bcfbaa192439f4da12c27282b17cf", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "1e879da48202ab8eca0d": "This is **Singapore**, captured at dusk or early evening with a stunning skyline reflected in the water.\n\nHere are the key visible landmarks and their positions:\n\n- **Marina Bay Sands (left)**: The iconic three-tower hotel complex topped by the SkyPark. It’s on the far left of the image, dominating the waterfront.\n  \n- **ArtScience Museum (center-left)**: The lotus-shaped building nestled between Marina Bay Sands and the central business district. It’s illuminated and sits just to the right of the Sands towers.\n\n- **Singapore Flyer (right)**: The giant observation wheel stands prominently on the right side of the frame, towering over surrounding buildings and offering panoramic views of the city.\n\n- **Central Business District skyline (center)**: A cluster of modern skyscrapers fills the middle ground, including recognizable structures like the UOB Plaza and other high-rises lit up against the twilight sky.\n\n- **Waterfront and reflections (foreground)**: The calm waters of Marina Bay mirror the city lights and structures, creating a serene and symmetrical composition.\n\nThe overall scene showcases Singapore’s blend of futuristic architecture, leisure attractions, and urban vibrancy — all set against a beautiful sunset sky.",
    "7b0fedf499c1ee41ce7e": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "1e879da48202ab8eca0d"}, "review": {"correctness": 40, "visual_detail": 30, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "clarity: extensive descriptive commentary and extra high-rise names exceed the requested brief position summary.", "answer_sha256": "6920592263909419eaaf365f19ded7ecca37b75b5bd506277dcdf2072914a56c", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
    "1f5b724968cd4e7b2e8f": "This scene is from the 1997 film **Titanic**, directed by James Cameron.\n\nIn this iconic moment, Jack Dawson (Leonardo DiCaprio) and Rose DeWitt Bukater (Kate Winslet) stand on the bow of the sinking ship, arms outstretched against a dramatic sunset. The ocean stretches beneath them, and the sky glows with warm orange and pink hues. Jack holds Rose from behind, his hands gently placed on her waist, while she looks ahead with an expression of awe and exhilaration — a rare moment of freedom and joy amid impending disaster. The scene captures their emotional bond and the film’s themes of love, loss, and transcendence.",
    "2434980087528350ce28": {"text": {"$ref": "image_answers", "id": "1f5b724968cd4e7b2e8f"}, "review": {"correctness": 39, "visual_detail": 29, "completeness": 20, "clarity": 8, "note": "correctness: calls the ship sinking, which the pictured scene does not show; clarity: adds plot/theme interpretation beyond the brief visible-scene request. Visual detail: the image-grounded feature is not described precisely.", "answer_sha256": "c384f6cde7eb0fd2e2720eadb988037a4cbad63d1d1bffaecaf27e6bed6feb04", "reviewer": "gpt-6-luna"}},
